"\nYou are observing a deterministic robot moving\nback and forth along a one-dimensional z-axis.\n\nThe robot moves at a fixed speed between two\nfixed patrol endpoints.\n\nAt the north endpoint, its stationary dwell\nduration alternates between two fixed values\non consecutive visits.\n\nAt the south endpoint, its stationary dwell\nduration remains constant.\n\nThe numerical endpoints, speed, dwell durations,\nand current alternation phase are unknown.\n\nNegative z direction means north.\nPositive z direction means south.\n\nTime t=0 is the current observation time.\nNo new observations are available after t=0.\n\nIf history is ordered, the positions are\nconsecutive chronological samples, ending one\nsample interval before the current observation.\n\nIf history is unordered, the positions are\nthe same historical samples with their temporal\norder removed.\n\nInfer the motion parameters and current latent\nphase from the available information.\n\nPredict the robot's future z-position at each\nrequested time.\n\nIf the information is insufficient to uniquely\ndetermine the future, explicitly acknowledge this.\n\nNevertheless, provide one best numerical\nprediction at each requested time.\n\nReturn only plain JSON with these fields:\n\n{\n  \"predictions\": [\n    {\n      \"time\": \"<requested time>\",\n      \"z\": \"<predicted position>\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"inferred_dynamics\": {\n    \"north_endpoint\": null,\n    \"south_endpoint\": null,\n    \"speed\": null,\n    \"north_dwell_values\": [],\n    \"south_dwell\": null,\n    \"last_north_dwell\": null,\n    \"next_north_dwell\": null\n  },\n  \"uncertainty\": \"brief explanation\"\n}\n\nUse numerical values where inferable.\nUse null for unknown parameters.\nInclude exactly one prediction per query time.\n"